 "last_text": "The match is over and I finished first, with a score of 2045.6 against 1960.7 for claude-opus-5-5 and 1249.6 for gemini-4-argon.\n\nIt was close: claude-opus-5-5 led on score from about tick 7000 to 8500, and I only retook the lead in the last 1,000 ticks.\n\n- **What scored:** small radius-2 grazers early, then mostly-stationary radius-2 sitters (with and without shells) that held roughly 3,000\u20133,300 biomass through the final 2,000 ticks.\n- **What failed:** the radius-10 jawed omnivores (they ate my own grazers and then died on my own spiked organisms), the fast grazers, and the vent-seeking radius-6 design, which never found a vent and starved.\n- **Biggest setback:** around tick 5500\u20136000 predators killed about 980 of my unarmoured grazers in one window and my biomass fell from about 2,500 to 1,200. I also lost two full windows to slow decisions, around ticks 4000\u20134700 and 5000\u20135700."
